      "claim": "A landlord cannot refuse housing based on the language spoken by the tenants.",
      "verdict": "supported"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Zurich is a multilingual and cosmopolitan city where many languages coexist (German, French, Italian, English, etc.).",
      "verdict": "supported"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Prioritizing a family based on language can be considered a form of discrimination and may violate tenancy law (Art. 262 and following of the Code of Obligations).",
      "verdict": "supported"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The choice must be based on objective and legal criteria (financial capacity, references, respect for tenancy rules, etc.) and not on the mother tongue of the candidates.",
